Lolly patch 0007: sing() asks Lolly for its models.

Why: upstream fetches the singing models from models.rondocode.com and
HuggingFace into the Cache API and loads ONNX Runtime's wasm from a CDN. The
frame has an opaque origin (no Cache API, no IndexedDB) and must never fetch
an external host. Every model byte now goes through ONE call to the utility
(src/lolly/sing.ts, lolly.singModels), by a stable file id in Lolly's `sing`
model family; ORT gets its wasm binary from the same call, one thread, no
proxy. The int8 builds are asked for first on every device. When the utility
has no models to give, the sung parts stay silent and an in-place notice
lists them instead of the bake error dialog; upstream's own download dialog
is not shown, because the utility makes the offer. Parts whose generated
vocals are loaded are tracked, with their voices and the parts left silent,
so a file made from the editor declares the AI-generated singing it holds.

Applied by scripts/vendor-rondocode.ts with git apply --directory=packages/rondo/upstream.

